content.content:
// that comes first alphabetically ("n/a" when nobody has a charge).
// The sheet's total yield is everyone's yield added together, leaving out anyone whose yield is "n/a".
// The sheet's grand flow is everyone's flow added together, leaving out anyone whose flow is "n/a".
// The sheet's top flow is the name of the person with the highest flow, ties going to the name
// that comes first alphabetically ("n/a" when nobody has a flow).
// Their norm is their scaled minus the median scaled of everyone on the sheet whose scaled can be
// worked out; for an even count, the lower of the two middle values ("n/a" while their scaled is "n/a").
// They are an outlier ("yes") when their norm is more than 100 away from zero in either direction, and
// otherwise "no" (also "no" while their norm is "n/a").
// Their stratum is TOP when their scaled is at or above the sheet's average (mean) scaled, otherwise BOT
// ("n/a" while their scaled is "n/a").
// The sheet's outlier count is how many of its people are outliers.
// Their ebb is their blend minus the mean blend of everyone on the sheet whose blend can be worked
// out, rounded down ("n/a" while their blend is "n/a").
// They are a stray ("yes") when their ebb is more than 100 away from zero in either direction, and
// otherwise "no" (also "no" while their ebb is "n/a").
// The sheet's stray count is how many of its people are strays.
// The sheet's final total is the sum of the scaled of its people whose state is FINAL, counting
// "n/a" as zero.
// The sheet's ledger is the grand total of everyone's scaled, leaving out anyone whose scaled is "n/a".
// The sheet's tier tally shows how many of its people are in each tier, SURGE, STEADY and SINK (zero when
// none are); people without a tier are not counted.
// The sheet's tier share shows, for each tier, SURGE, STEADY and SINK, its tally as a percentage of the
// sheet's headcount, rounded down ("n/a" when the sheet has nobody on it).
// The sheet's tier ledger shows the total momentum of its people in each tier, SURGE, STEADY and SINK (zero
// when none are); people without a tier add nothing.
// The sheet's top per tier shows, for each tier, SURGE, STEADY and SINK, the name of the person in it with
// the highest scaled, ties going to the name earlier in the alphabet ("n/a" when none of them have a scaled).
// The sheet's stratum counts show how many of its people are in each stratum, TOP and BOT (zero when
// none are); people whose stratum is "n/a" are not counted.
// The sheet's band counts show how many of its people are in each band, A through E (zero when none
// are); people whose band is "n/a" are not counted.
// The sheet's span width is how many different bands have at least one of its people in them.
// The sheet's drag counts show how many of its people are in each drag level, L0 through L3 (zero when
// none are); people whose drag is "n/a" are not counted.
// The sheet's pulse counts show how many of its people have each pulse, NEG, FLAT and POS (zero when
// none do); people whose pulse is "n/a" are not counted.
// The sheet's bracket counts show how many of its people are in each bracket, Q4 down to Q1 (zero when
// none are); people whose bracket is "n/a" are not counted.
// The sheet's grade tally shows how many of its people have each grade, HIGH and LOW (zero when none
// do), with MID folded into HIGH; MID is still listed but always counts zero. People without a grade
// are not counted.
// The sheet's grade share shows, for each grade, LOW, MID and HIGH, how many of its people have it (MID
// counted as itself) as a percentage of the sheet's headcount, rounded down ("n/a" when the sheet has
// nobody on it).
// The sheet's grade ledger shows the total scaled of its people with each grade, HIGH and LOW (zero
// when none do), with MID folded into HIGH; MID is still listed but always totals zero. It counts "n/a"
// as zero; people without a grade add nothing.
// The sheet's top per grade shows, for each grade, LOW, MID and HIGH, the name of the person with it with
// the highest scaled, ties going to the name earlier in the alphabet ("n/a" when none of them have a scaled).
// The sheet's state tally shows how many of its people are in each state, DRAFT, REVIEW, FINAL and
// REWORK (zero when none are).
// The sheet's top per state shows, for each state, DRAFT, REVIEW, FINAL and REWORK, the name of the person
// in it with the highest scaled, ties going to the name earlier in the alphabet ("n/a" when none of them
// have a scaled).
// The sheet's state ledger shows, for each state, the total scaled of its people in it, counting "n/a" as
// zero. Only FINAL and REVIEW are totalled; DRAFT and REWORK are still listed but always total zero.
// The sheet's state share shows what percent of its people are in each state, rounded down (zero when
// the sheet has no people).
// The sheet's groups are listed by name, with a form to add one. Each person is in one group, chosen on
// add, through Edit or on the row, and the row shows its name.
// Each group shows its strength: the sum of the effective of the people in it, counting "n/a" as zero.
// The sheet's biggest group is the name of the group with the highest strength, ties going to the name
// that comes first alphabetically ("n/a" when there are no groups).
// The sheet's prime group is the name of its strongest group: the same group as its biggest group
// ("n/a" when there are no groups).
// The sheet's top group size is the size of its biggest group ("n/a" when there are no groups).
// The sheet's total strength is the sum of the strengths of all its groups (0 when there are none).
// The sheet's group count is how many groups it has (0 when there are none).
